From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add DS video

vid_nds.c shows the 3D view on the top screen with a text layer over it
for the messages: Quake's font as 8bpp tiles in VRAM bank F and a 32x24
map in bank E, with the tiles of the loading plaque, which shows on black
while a level loads, with menu layers hidden and game text cleared. The
touch screen keeps the startup console until the first level is ready. Edge marking
makes the hardware fill the edges of the
3D polygons, which it leaves gaps along otherwise, all with the same
polygon ID so none is marked, antialiasing blended them with the
background. The frame is depth tested on w.

The touch screen shows the rest of Quake's 2D drawing in a 320x200
buffer, copied into an 8bpp bitmap background in VRAM bank C and scaled
to 256x192 by the affine background hardware, smoothed by a second layer
half a pixel further that is alpha blended on top (vid_smooth). The menu
draws into the same buffer, its rows get back what the touch screen shows
from VRAM when something draws there again: it's cut into 8x8 tiles for
the same layers on the top screen, scrolled to center it, its 255
transparent and Quake's black moved there. Only the tiles with something
on them take VRAM, the rest of bank E, the texture palette moved to bank
G for it. A tile keeps its slot while it shows the same picture, changed
ones go to slots the shown map doesn't use and the new map shows at the
next vblank, so no tile is seen while it's written. The draw functions mark the rows they
change, only those are copied, and the touch screen can keep rows drawn,
VID_BeginUI tells it when something else drew over them. The palette
goes to both screens, the texture palette and the particle colors, so
palette shifts for damage and pickups tint everything for free. vid_showfps shows the frame
rate.
---
